    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0830" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v16/pg796"/>

                <head>366. Telegram From the Embassy in Laos to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d366-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vientiane</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-08-15T20:00:00+07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                                1960—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>294. Addressees pass to interested agencies. Ref: Deptel 171.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d366-f2"/> We have received request from Phoumi for 10 million kip
                    to help him retake Vientiane and statement he plans drop tracts over Vientiane
                    today telling of resistance. Based on reftel we have instructed [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not declassified</hi>]
                    PEO representatives Savannakhet as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“You should advise PhoumiUS is not at this stage prepared support him in
                            forcible effort (A) retake Vientiane or (B) prevent establishment new
                            government. He should not drop tracts Vientiane. This based on specific
                            instructions from Washington.”<anchor n="3" xml:id="d366-f3"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Brown</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d366-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d366-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 751J.00/8–1560. Secret; Limit
                    Distribution. Repeated to Bangkok, Saigon, Phnom Penh, and CINCPAC for POLAD.
                    Received at 1:35 p.m.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d366-f2" n="2" xml:id="d366-f2-content">
                <p>Printed as telegram 172 to Bangkok, <ref target="#d364">Document 364</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d366-f3" n="3" xml:id="d366-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram 176 to Vientiane, August 15, the Department informed the Embassy that
                    this message was approved. (Department of State, Central Files, 751J.00/8–1560)
                    In telegram 298 from Vientiane, August 16, 10 a.m., Brown reported that an
                    Embassy official delivered the message to Phoumi at 4 a.m. on August 16, and
                    that “Phoumi nodded politely but said he would proceed with his original plan”
                    to take Vientiane by force. (<hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., 751J.00/8–1660;
                    included in <ref target="frus1958-60v15-16mSupp1">the microfiche
                        supplement</ref>) Phoumi’s plan to retake Vientiane is described in a
                    telegram from Felt to JCS, 162113Z August. (Department of State, Central Files,
                    751J.00/8–1660; included in <ref target="frus1958-60v15-16mSupp1">the microfiche
                        supplement</ref>)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
